## Verification
- Every phase: gofmt -l . (empty), go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -race ./... all green.
- Mutation checks: disabling rollback makes the fault-injection tests fail (refs/index/status/files reported); removing the parent gate makes TestParentGate fail; removing the .users scan skip makes TestUsersDirIgnoredByScans fail.
- Fault injection fails every mutating git step in turn (start: 3-4 steps, complete: 11 per layout across 3 flows, restart: 3 per variant) and asserts full state restoration, in all 5 tasks-dir layouts.
- Manual end-to-end scenario with the built CLI in a scratch code repo + separate tasks repo: start -> wip; complete -m -> one-commit final; reopen + base advance + start -> replayed; forced conflict -> clean error, byte-identical state; subtask merged then parent delivered; obsolete -> safety commit and return to base; tasks repo untouched; web board shows chips, copy buttons, Git block, app.js served.

## Deviations from the plan
- P3: Snapshot handles a gitignored tasks dir explicitly (git add rejects an exclude pathspec naming an ignored directory): add unexcluded, then reset the tasks path to HEAD in the temp index; check-ignore uses --no-index. The replay "unsupported" detection keys on "unknown option" / "is not a git command" (usage text always contains "ref-action").
- P5: start/complete record writes now run through the journal (failed parent auto-start/auto-complete also rolls back); a non-delivered cascade also clears a pointer naming a cascaded subtask.
- P6: vcs.FirstExistingBranch returns an empty name (no error) when none exists. A todo parent starting fresh allows carrying uncommitted changes from the base (the subtask lands on the base tip).
- P8: restart skips the checkpoint when HEAD is already the task's wip and nothing needs replaying. Parent-line resolution (fresh start / in-place restart of a todo parent) is shared by the subtask start and restart paths.
- P9: CLI complete prints "Final branch: X." or "Merged into <parent wip>." for delivered completions only (the CLI cannot read HEAD).
- Flow code is split across branching_start.go / branching_complete.go / branching_restart.go instead of one branching.go.

